 -2, 0, -5, -3, -3, 2, -3 | -9]\nR6: [-1, -3, -1, -4, 0, 1, 2, 2, -1, 8 | -3]\nR7: [2, 4, 0, 5, 8, 0, -2, 1, -2, -7 | -7]\nR8: [0, -2, 0, -2, 2, -3, -10, 5, 9, -1 | 2]\nR9: [2, 3, -4, 4, -2, 2, -3, 4, 3, -2 | -1]\nR10: [2, 2, -4, 1, 2, 5, 2, 5, -1, -1 | 2]\n\nI notice there are many zeros in first column. R1 has -1, R2 0, R3 0, R4 -2, R5 -2, R6 -1, R7 2, R8 0, R9 2, R10 2. We can use R1 as pivot. Multiply R1 by -1 to make pivot 1: new R1 = -R1: [1,2,-1,2,0,2,2,-1,-2,-2 | -5]. But careful: original R1: [-1,-2,1,-2,0,-2,-2,1,2,2 | 5]. Multiply by -1 gives [1,2,-1,2,0,2,2,-1,-2,-2 | -5]. So let's set R1' = -R1.\n\nNow eliminate first column from other rows that have non-zero. R4: [-2,-4,1,-5,-2,-2,-1,2,2,6 | -9]. Add 2*R1' to R4? Actually we want to eliminate the first column. R4 has -2, so add 2*R1' to R4: 2*[1,2,-1,2,0,2,2,-1,-2,-2] = [2,4,-2,4,0,4,4,-2,-4,-4] plus R4 gives [0,0,-1,-1,-2,2,3,0,-2,2 | -9+(-10)? Wait: b: R4 b=-9, R1' b=-5, so add 2*(-5) = -10 gives -19? Let's compute carefully: R4 after adding 2*R1': newR4 = R4 + 2*R1' = (col1: -2+2=0; col2: -4+4=0; col3: 1+(-2)=-1; col4: -5+4=-1; col5: -2+0=-2; col6: -2+4=2; col7: -1+4=3; col8: 2+(-2)=0; col9: 2+(-4)=-2; col10: 6+(-4)=2; b: -9+2*(-5)=-9-10=-19). So new R4: [0,0,-1,-1,-2,2,3,0,-2,2 | -19].\n\nR5: [-2,-2,5,-2,0,-5,-3,-3,2,-3 | -9]. Add 2*R1': gives [0,2,3,2,0,-1,1,-5,0,-7 | -9+(-10)=-19]? Actually compute: col1: -2+2=0; col2: -2+4=2; col3: 5+(-2)=3; col4: -2+4=2; col5: 0+0=0; col6: -5+4=-1; col7: -3+4=1; col8: -3+(-2)=-5; col9: 2+(-4)=-2? Wait careful: R1' col9 = -2, so 2*(-2) = -4, R5 col9=2, sum = -2; col10: -3+(-4)=-7; b: -9+2*(-5)=-19. So new R5: [0,2,3,2,0,-1,1,-5,-2,-7 | -19].\n\nR6: [-1,-3,-1,-4,0,1,2,2,-1,8 | -3]. Add 1*R1' (since -1+1=0). Actually R6 col1 = -1, so add R1': newR6 = R6 + R1' = [0,-1,-2,-2,0,3,4,1,-3,6 | -3+(-5)=-8]. Compute: col1: -1+1=0; col2: -3+2=-1; col3: -1+(-1)=-2; col4: -4+2=-2; col5: 0+0=0; col6: 1+2=3; col7: 2+2=4; col8: 2+(-1)=1; col9: -1+(-2)=-3; col10: 8+(-2)=6; b: -3+(-5)=-8. So new R6: [0,-1,-2,-2,0,3,4,1,-3,6 | -8].\n\nR7: [2,4,0,5,8,0,-2,1,-2,-7 | -7]. Subtract 2*R1'? Actually to eliminate first column, we want to make col1 0. R7 col1 =2, so subtract 2*R1': newR7 = R7 - 2*R1' = [0,0,2,1,8,-4,-6,3,2,-3 | -7 -2*(-5)= -7+10=3]. Compute: col1:2-2=0; col2:4-4=0; col3:0-(-2)=2? Actually 0 - 2*(-1)=0+2=2; col4:5-2*2=5-4=1; col5:8-0=8; col6:0-2*2=0-4=-4; col7:-2-2*2=-2-4=-6; col8:1-2*(-1)=1+2=3; col9:-2-2*(-2)=-2+4=2; col10:-7-2*(-2)=-7+4=-3; b:-7 - 2*(-5)= -7+10=3. So new R7: [0,0,2,1,8,-4,-6,3,2,-3 | 3].\n\nR8: [0,-2,0,-2,2,-3,-10,5,9,-1 | 2]. First column already 0, no change.\n\nR9: [2,3,-4,4,-2,2,-3,4,3,-2 | -1]. Subtract 2*R1' (since 2-2=0): newR9 = R9 - 2*R1' = [0,-1,-2,0,-2,-2,-7,6,7,2 | -1 -2*(-5)= -1+10=9]. Compute: col1:2-2=0; col2:3-4=-1; col3:-4-(-2)= -4+2=-2? Actually 2*R1' col3 = 2*(-1)=-2, so -4 - (-2)= -4+2=-2; col4:4-4=0; col5:-2-0=-2; col6:2-4=-2; col7:-3-4=-7; col8:4-(-2)=4+2=6; col9:3-(-4)=3+4=7; col10:-2-(-4)=-2+4=2; b:-1 -2*(-5)=-1+10=9. So new R9: [0,-1,-2,0,-2,-2,-7,6,7,2 | 9].\n\nR10: [2,2,-4,1,2,5,2,5,-1,-1 | 2]. Subtract 2*R1': newR10 = R10 - 2*R1' = [0,-2,-2,-3,2,1,-2,7,3,3 | 2-2*(-5)=2+10=12]. Compute: col1:2-2=0; col2:2-4=-2; col3:-4-(-2)= -4+2=-2; col4:1-4=-3; col5:2-0=2; col6:5-4=1; col7:2-4=-2; col8:5-(-2)=5+2=7; col9:-1-(-4)= -1+4=3; col10:-1-(-4)= -1+4=3; b:2-2*(-5)=2+10=12. So new R10: [0,-2,-2,-3,2,1,-2,7,3,3 | 12].\n\nNow we have updated rows (R2, R3 unchanged? R2 and R3 already had 0 in first column, so they stay same. But we should note R2 and R3 are as original. Let's list all rows after first elimination:\n\nR1': [1,2,-1,2,0,2,2,-1,-2,-2 | -5] (pivot row)\nR2: [0,-1,-1,-1,0,0,-2,2,2,2 | 6]\nR3: [0,-2,-1,-2,2,-1,-6,4,5,2 | 8]\nR4': [0,0,-1,-1,-2,2,3,0,-2,2 | -19]\nR5': [0,2,3,2,0,-1,1,-5,-2,-7 | -19]\nR6': [0,-1,-2,-2,0,3,4,1,-3,6 | -8]\nR7': [0,0,2,1,8,-4,-6,3,2,-3 | 3]\nR8: [0,-2,0,-2,2,-3,-10,5,9,-1 | 2]\nR9': [0,-1,-2,0,-2,-2,-7,6,7,2 | 9]\nR10': [0,-2,-2,-3,2,1,-2,7,3,3 | 12]\n\nNow we 